  "step_3": "The decision reason requires computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes and evaluating lotteries by the probability of exceeding this level. The individual does not reference any such calculation or concept. While both the reason and the individual consider outcome levels and probabilities, the specific mechanism—calculating a mean outcome and assessing positive deviations—is absent in the verbal report. The individual’s focus is on avoiding zero and gaining as much or more than the sure amount, which aligns more with satisficing or regret avoidance than the defined aspiration-level rule. There is no evidence that the aspiration level was computed or used to assess positive differences. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
