  "step_2": "The individual considers the certainty of winning in Lottery B (100% chance) as more attractive than the risk of getting nothing in Lottery A (20% chance of 0 Euros). The individual also mentions that the difference in potential winnings between A (4000) and B (3000) is not large enough to justify taking the risk associated with A. The justification focuses on risk aversion and the appeal of guaranteed outcomes, rather than on comparing outcomes to a reference point derived from all possible outcomes. The individual does not mention any calculation or consideration of an average outcome level, nor do they evaluate which lottery exceeds or falls short of such a level more frequently. The deliberation centers on certainty and perceived insufficient reward for risk, not on deviations from an aspiration level.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating outcomes relative to an aspiration level (2333.33 Euros) and comparing the probabilities of exceeding this level. However, the individual does not reference such a level or any comparison of outcomes to a computed average. Instead, the individual emphasizes the security of a sure win in B and judges the 1000 Euro difference between 4000 and 3000 as insufficient to accept risk. This reflects a risk-averse or certainty-based heuristic, not the aspiration-level rule. There is no evidence that the individual computed or implicitly used the mean of all outcomes as a reference point. The justification is based on a different rationale. Therefore, the decision reason based on aspiration level and positive differences is not reflected in the verbal report.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
